{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408145-qwixalted-and-exalted","id":1408145,"title":"Qwixalted and Exalted?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-14T06:59:10-07:00","id":1408145,"title":"Qwixalted and Exalted?","content":"I was wondering if anyone here had heard of 'Qwixalted' before and had success in running it? It's basically a homebrew rules lite version of Exalted.<br /> <br /> I found it was a little overwhelming teaching my group 3E and have been thoroughly informed of how difficult 2.5e and 1e is to run. With Essence still in the works, 'Qwixalted Extended' served me really well for a campaign so far, though not without careful rereading. It's deceptively complex.Then I found out there's three other versions of Qwixalted, by a user called Daiklave, one called Jarvis and another by Aakin, stretching back 10 years or so. Has anyone here had success in any of them or thought about running them?<br /> <br /> EDIT: <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://anonymousfiles.io/GxlqSxln/\" target=\"_blank\">https://anonymousfiles.io/GxlqSxln/</a> this is the latest Qwixalted Extended edition as far as I know. Still a few problems with wording here and there, because it talks about 'Control spells' without telling you what those are. Someone should offer to go through and edit it for him so that it reads better, because there's some seriously innovative stuff in here that's a little marred by its haphazardness. <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://s2.desu-usergeneratedcontent.xyz/tg/image/1596/10/1596109848941.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">https://s2.desu-usergeneratedcontent...6109848941.pdf</a> Someone else made this but the creator said it looked fine. I don't recognise some of the charm names here, so it might be from older editions too.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26024,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","user":"Distant Choir","date":".  Updated with Links 08-17-2020, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T15:32:47-07:00","id":1408260,"title":"","content":"Yes i have. The last campaign i ran, i ran on Qwixalted. I bounced off 3e quite hard and decided to run a campaign in a lighter system. I was going to run it on Fate Legends of Anglierre, but one of my players vetoed as he hates FATE. So i did some digging and it came down to godbound and qwixalted and i went with Qwix.<br /> <br /> I made some changes of my own to the system, and added stuff from godbound. I liked it but my players never really pushed the system to its limits. Personally , i think with the changes i made it has become my go to for a Exalted game, at least until Essence comes out.<br /> <br /> So i think it makes a good placeholder for rules light until Essence arrives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T22:44:54-07:00","id":1408315,"title":"","content":"Qwixalted Extended is the most 3e-esque version, made by someone on /tg/ if I recall. I have yet to use it, but it looks pretty good for what it sets out to do. My biggest issue is that it's not entirely clear how exactly some things work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24587-yamajin","name":"Yamajin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24587_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T03:30:07-07:00","id":1408327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yamajin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408145-qwixalted-and-exalted?p=1408315#post1408315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Qwixalted Extended is the most 3e-esque version, made by someone on /tg/ if I recall. I have yet to use it, but it looks pretty good for what it sets out to do. My biggest issue is that it's not entirely clear how exactly some things work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, there's a few 4chanisms in it but i'm running Qwixalted Extended and am having a blast, but since I think it's just one guy writing it some parts are a little difficult to understand. I think the hardest thing for me to 'get' when I started was how Traits worked, because I didn't realise it's Attributes OR Abilities rather than Attributes + Abilities","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T13:15:56-07:00","id":1408402,"title":"","content":"I made that same mistake at first. One other thing with that split is that I'm not sure what Attribute is supposed to govern ranged attacks. Is it still Strength? Dex? Perception? It definitely needs more examples of what exactly constitutes a proper use of Ways, or how Gifts are supposed to work exactly. One of the examples for the Paced Way is that you strike a blow that leaves a lasting wound- but what does that actually do? Just make it take longer to heal? I have no idea how Power is supposed to work and I go cross-eyed trying to figure out Sorcery.<br /> <br /> All that said, if he cleared some stuff up and gave some more examples of how to make charms and gifts, maybe with some sample charms to flesh things out, I think it'd be an excellent book overall. I'd like to try it out myself sometime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24587-yamajin","name":"Yamajin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24587_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T14:45:07-07:00","id":1408411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yamajin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408145-qwixalted-and-exalted?p=1408402#post1408402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made that same mistake at first. One other thing with that split is that I'm not sure what Attribute is supposed to govern ranged attacks. Is it still Strength? Dex? Perception? It definitely needs more examples of what exactly constitutes a proper use of Ways, or how Gifts are supposed to work exactly. One of the examples for the Paced Way is that you strike a blow that leaves a lasting wound- but what does that actually do? Just make it take longer to heal? I have no idea how Power is supposed to work and I go cross-eyed trying to figure out Sorcery.<br /> <br /> All that said, if he cleared some stuff up and gave some more examples of how to make charms and gifts, maybe with some sample charms to flesh things out, I think it'd be an excellent book overall. I'd like to try it out myself sometime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're totally right on that part on the Attributes and certainly on the Sorcery/Gifts thing, because sometimes it's unclear how 'specific' it's supposed to be. <br /> <br /> <br /> He released a new version and I believe someone wrote a mock up of some Solar Charm conversions. If you'd like, I can send them to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T20:49:24-07:00","id":1408452,"title":"","content":"I'd appreciate that a lot, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24587-yamajin","name":"Yamajin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24587_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T06:19:45-07:00","id":1408480,"title":"","content":"Sent! :P I'd be interested if Essence uses a similar 'Size' system and the like, since it's really useful for representing a lot of different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T01:10:00-07:00","id":1408668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Distant Choir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408145-qwixalted-and-exalted?p=1408480#post1408480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sent! :P I'd be interested if Essence uses a similar 'Size' system and the like, since it's really useful for representing a lot of different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you send it to me too? I find the idea interesting, but I find it almost unplayable with the base rules. Especially sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T01:47:10-07:00","id":1408671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shapechanger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408145-qwixalted-and-exalted?p=1408668#post1408668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you send it to me too? I find the idea interesting, but I find it almost unplayable with the base rules. Especially sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've updated the OP with both the links, since I sort of realised that neither of those creators actually care who posts it where. Unfortunately since they're anonymous, I can't give much credit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T03:10:49-07:00","id":1408683,"title":"","content":"Very appreciated. I must admit that it's far more clear in the last update. At least, I finally understood how Sorcery is actually used.<br /> <br /> But I have to say that I don't particularly appreciate the use of just Attributes or Skill in the rolls. Especially since a lot of things related to Sorcery or Thaumaturgy relay only on Occult and there is no indication on how they're supposed to work for Attribute-based Exalts like Lunars or Infernals. Which especially for Infernals is jarring because they can learn Third Circle Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I still don't get how an Infernal's Affinity and Ways are supposed to interact. A little help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T04:12:03-07:00","id":1408687,"title":"","content":"No worries. In the Sorcery part for Workings, it mentions to roll Occult/Int, so you use that for the Shaping rolls. I admit, I kind of think it's a bit too much of a sacred cow that the Abilities/Attributes are divided up like this since there's other instances where it's a little messy...but then again, I wouldn't know how to fix that without a complete rewrite of Abilities/Attributes in general. Maybe it's around for conversion purposes?<br /> <br /> On the Infernal Affinity thing, I actually had to check a 4chan thread where he clarifies it, yikes! Basically from what he indicated, Affinities and Ways decide what themes you're allowed to cover when you buy those Ways 'normally'. They're basically Yozi domains you have to align by, so let's use an Infernal with the Ebon Dragon as an Affinity for example.<br /> <br /> So the reason it gives you all the Ways for your base Affinity is so that you automatically get to cover those themes with the Ways you buy. However, in this example where you have an Affinity to the Ebon Dragon, you can't do certain things like conjure light, fire or use a charm that's overly brazen / unsubtle. However, if you purchase an Affinity in something like Supernatural from Malfeas, your themes can cover things of Malfeas' affinity that would otherwise be disbarred if you had only the Ebon Dragon's affinity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T04:34:35-07:00","id":1408689,"title":"","content":"So you have to buy Ways for every affinity aside for the native one separatedly? Seem likes a lot of exp has to go there for Infernals.<br /> <br /> I suppose that's another reason they went with Attribuites instead of Skills. More versatility with a single purchase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T06:45:08-07:00","id":1408703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shapechanger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408145-qwixalted-and-exalted?p=1408689#post1408689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you have to buy Ways for every affinity aside for the native one separatedly? Seem likes a lot of exp has to go there for Infernals.<br /> <br /> I suppose that's another reason they went with Attribuites instead of Skills. More versatility with a single purchase.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not quite. Basically the way it works is that any actual Ways you purchase for an Attribute can be used with any Affinity you know. So if you know the Supernatural Dexterity Way and have both the Malfeas and Adorjan Supernatural Affinities, you can use the Dexterity Way in any way that would match either of those Affinities, without having to completely repurchase the Supernatural Dexterity Way. Affinities are generally cheaper to purchase than Ways, so it's not quite as bad as having to repurchase every Way for each Affinity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24587-yamajin","name":"Yamajin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24587_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T06:47:02-07:00","id":1408704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yamajin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408145-qwixalted-and-exalted?p=1408703#post1408703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not quite. Basically the way it works is that any actual Ways you purchase for an Attribute can be used with any Affinity you know. So if you know the Supernatural Dexterity Way and have both the Malfeas and Adorjan Supernatural Affinities, you can use the Dexterity Way in any way that would match either of those Affinities, without having to completely repurchase the Supernatural Dexterity Way. Affinities are generally cheaper to purchase than Ways, so it's not quite as bad as having to repurchase every Way for each Affinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that so? Well, better for the Infernals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T01:53:45-07:00","id":1409092,"title":"","content":"Infernals look pretty fun to play, but definitely seem a little gated behind the Shintai's when it comes to Improvised Charms. <br /> <br /> So far, none of my players have managed to find a stupidly overpowered build to break the game but I guess time will tell in that department. I have a small hunch that the Solar 'Zeal' Endowment coupled with Triumphant is something that is very, very powerful. Either that or some clever use of Crafting, since I don't think there's any RPG system out there where Crafting isn't sleeper powerful lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T02:10:57-07:00","id":1409096,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's just me, but I think the most broken thing about Qwixalted is the Paced Way. Not only you can make effects that last years or decades (potentially forever, and just with a Celestial Working if I read the whole thing right) but you can also drastically reduce intervals times. At character creation, you can make a Charm to reduce the interval for Extended Actions by three -potentially fire or six- whole categories for 1 mote. Three categories mean years become days, or days become rounds, or something equally ridiculous. It sounds pretty abusable, especially combined with Sorcery and Artifact creation.<br /> <br /> And that's just character creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T02:40:40-07:00","id":1409098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shapechanger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408145-qwixalted-and-exalted?p=1409096#post1409096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's just me, but I think the most broken thing about Qwixalted is the Paced Way. Not only you can make effects that last years or decades (potentially forever, and just with a Celestial Working if I read the whole thing right) but you can also drastically reduce intervals times. At character creation, you can make a Charm to reduce the interval for Extended Actions by three -potentially fire or six- whole categories for 1 mote. Three categories mean years become days, or days become rounds, or something equally ridiculous. It sounds pretty abusable, especially combined with Sorcery and Artifact creation.<br /> <br /> And that's just character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The only quibble there is that the rules stipulates that things that matter in combat do it for (X) turns rather than (X) narrative time. So while you could likely make a Charm that lets your Solar use an Essence Sword for a day or longer as you level up, you couldn't use Overwhelming + Triumphant + Supernatural 3 to have that last for millennia. It lasts for at maximum six turns if your Solar has six Essence.<br /> <br /> For things like reducing certain actions, there's still Scale Based Minimums which must be adhered to unless you have another charm that ignores it. Even if it's something like reflexively healing yourself, you'd still need to have Supernatural in addition to Paced to make sure you ignore your own wound penalty. And if it's an Improvised Charm, it's 3 motes. For clarity, a Solar without the Cult background starts at 11 Motes. <br /> <br /> by the way, how do you manage to reduce the Interval by more than 3 steps? The (X) value is always limited by Essence and you start at Essence 3. Do you mean you get Gift Points to improve your Way by +1 for a single Named Charm/Evocation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T02:56:34-07:00","id":1409099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Distant Choir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408145-qwixalted-and-exalted?p=1409098#post1409098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only quibble there is that the rules stipulates that things that matter in combat do it for (X) turns rather than (X) narrative time. So while you could likely make a Charm that lets your Solar use an Essence Sword for a day or longer as you level up, you couldn't use Overwhelming + Triumphant + Supernatural 3 to have that last for millennia. It lasts for at maximum six turns if your Solar has six Essence.<br /> <br /> For things like reducing certain actions, there's still Scale Based Minimums which must be adhered to unless you have another charm that ignores it. Even if it's something like reflexively healing yourself, you'd still need to have Supernatural in addition to Paced to make sure you ignore your own wound penalty. And if it's an Improvised Charm, it's 3 motes. For clarity, a Solar without the Cult background starts at 11 Motes.</div> </div> </div> </div>In-combat use of long duration charms is in fact limited, but out-of-combat is not. You said that crafting is sleeping-OP in most games. I agree completely, I think every Extended Action is OP under Qwixalted with the right charm. Considerin each Charm can have up to Essence Ways, it's not impossible to simply dish out Artifacts and Workings to give you a lot of bonuses. I should read the rules better to be sure, but 3 Ways seem more than enough as a start to do... pretty much everything you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Distant Choir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408145-qwixalted-and-exalted?p=1409098#post1409098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">by the way, how do you manage to reduce the Interval by more than 3 steps? The (X) value is always limited by Essence and you start at Essence 3. Do you mean you get Gift Points to improve your Way by +1 for a single Named Charm/Evocation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely forgot that there was a limit equal to Essence. I suppose that you can't reduce the steps by five or six right at character creation.<br /> <br /> But Artifacts and Workings can do it. Since they give (or can with spells? I'm not sure) Gifts and one of the Gifts does improve a Way, I'm sure you can munchkin your way to even faster steps.<br /> <br /> That said, I didn't read the text in-depth because it's still hard to read and a little confusing, so I could be misremembering something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T09:39:14-07:00","id":1409156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shapechanger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408145-qwixalted-and-exalted?p=1409099#post1409099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In-combat use of long duration charms is in fact limited, but out-of-combat is not. You said that crafting is sleeping-OP in most games. I agree completely, I think every Extended Action is OP under Qwixalted with the right charm. Considerin each Charm can have up to Essence Ways, it's not impossible to simply dish out Artifacts and Workings to give you a lot of bonuses. I should read the rules better to be sure, but 3 Ways seem more than enough as a start to do... pretty much everything you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's a limit to the amount of Gift points(bonuses) you can have (Resistance+Essence) from any source ingrained in you and Artifacts still need Sources, things you have to go out and get. Perhaps I was being a bit disingenuous when I called it Sleeper OP to begin with, since on reflection it still requires legwork and such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shapechanger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408145-qwixalted-and-exalted?p=1409099#post1409099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I completely forgot that there was a limit equal to Essence. I suppose that you can't reduce the steps by five or six right at character creation.<br /> <br /> But Artifacts and Workings can do it. Since they give (or can with spells? I'm not sure) Gifts and one of the Gifts does improve a Way, I'm sure you can munchkin your way to even faster steps.<br /> <br /> That said, I didn't read the text in-depth because it's still hard to read and a little confusing, so I could be misremembering something.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could do that, but then we get back to 'Workings' and 'Artifacts' needing a Foci and Sources to begin with, so while it is certainly not something to sneeze at, there's still some balance there. And you'd definitely be narrowing your focus big time, which may not pan out the way you think in terms of how OP something is.<br /> <br /> Honestly I feel like there's a lot of sections in the book where it could be cleaned up a little. I suppose I could try my hand at it, but I'd feel icky doing that to someone else's work without their permission and I have no way to reach out to the guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T11:04:37-07:00","id":1409388,"title":"","content":"Its a chan work. Just make the edits and post it in a thread with a comment like &quot;Fixed it for you, &quot; and 9 people will be like &quot;based.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T18:05:16-07:00","id":1409441,"title":"","content":"If you'd really like to ask his permission I think he typically hangs out in the /exg/ threads, so you can just ask in there and he'll hopefully respond at some point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24587-yamajin","name":"Yamajin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24587_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T01:45:13-07:00","id":1409717,"title":"","content":"I might do at some point once work gets off my back, I've never posted there before so it's a little nerve wracking &gt;_&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T13:20:10-07:00","id":1410121,"title":"","content":"Is there a chance of anybody reuploading the new version of Qwixalted Extended to a page that doesn't make my antivirus scream at me very loudly? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24670-ufnal","name":"Ufnal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T14:50:49-07:00","id":1410135,"title":"","content":"I can give a 4chan link for it. I haven't personally had issues with that website but I can understand the apprehension.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://s1.desu-usergeneratedcontent.xyz/tg/image/1596/88/1596880633080.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"htt